cants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIZAWA TAKATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OJI YUKA SYNT PAPER CO LTD</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIINA MASAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANIGUCHI HIRONOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIZAWA, TAKATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OJI-YUKA SYNTHETIC PAPER CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIINA, MASAKI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANIGUCHI, HIRONOBU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIZAWA TAKATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIINA MASAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TANIGUCHI HIRONOBU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIZAWA, TAKATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIINA, MASAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TANIGUCHI, HIRONOBU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A label for in-mold molding comprising a base layer (I) consisting of a thermoplastic resin film and a heat-sealable resin layer (II) formed on the back side of the layer (I), wherein the layer (II) comprises a polyethylene resin and at least one of (i) a fatty acid amide having a molecular weight of 300 or larger and (ii) fine (in)organic particles having an average particle diameter larger than the thickness of the layer (II).  The label is excellent in suitability for paper feeding/discharging during printing and in workability in cutting, can be easily inserted into a mold during in-mold molding, and gives a labeled container which is free from blistering and has high fusion strength between the container and the label.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une étiquette pour le moulage en moule, comprenant une couche de base (I) constituée d'une pellicule de résine thermoplastique et une couche de résine thermoscellable (II) formée sur l'envers de la couche (I). La couche (II) comprend une résine de polyéthylène et au moins (i) un amide d'acide gras possédant un poids moléculaire de 300 ou plus, ou (ii) des fines particules inorganiques possédant un diamètre de particule moyen supérieur à l'épaisseur de la couche (II). Ladite étiquette convient parfaitement à la décharge/fourniture de papier pendant l'impression et peut être modifiée facilement pendant le processus de coupe, peut être insérée facilement dans un moule pendant le moulage en moule et permet la production d'un récipient à étiquette exempt de cloquage, une résistance à la fusion élevée entre le récipient et l'étiquette étant en outre assurée.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>